Package: rbfkernel
Type: Package
Title: RBF (Gaussian) Kernel Methods with Fast Exact Tuning Workflows
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("lunganlungpg", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "lunganlungpg@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Readable implementations of the radial basis function (Gaussian)
    kernel, bandwidth heuristics, kernel ridge regression and classification,
    random Fourier features and the Nystroem approximation. Kernel ridge models
    are tuned with exact leave-one-out cross-validation computed from one
    eigendecomposition per bandwidth, so a whole gamma by lambda grid costs
    about as much as a single fit. A one-call workflow takes any data frame and
    a target column, detects classification or regression, scales the
    features, tunes the model, evaluates it on held-out data, and exports
    tables and plots. Optional support for RBF support vector machines via
    'e1071'.
